WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.634
Hi, I'm Sheave!

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.174
This agent has no policy.

00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:07.871
It has a model that proposes whole plans, and it learns from

00:00:07.871 --> 00:00:09.719
the plans its own search finds.

00:00:11.558 --> 00:00:15.497
Sample whole action sequences from a diffusion model, improve them by search,

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:17.466
then teach the model the winners.

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:25.322
The state goes into a diffusion model over whole action sequences.

00:00:25.322 --> 00:00:26.860
It samples thirty-two plans.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.519
A beam search copies the best few and re-noises only their uncommitted

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:32.932
actions, then denoises them.

00:00:33.352 --> 00:00:37.393
Five learned dynamics models roll each plan forward, and a reward model

00:00:37.393 --> 00:00:39.077
and value function score it.

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:42.804
Repeat once per step of the horizon, then execute the first

00:00:42.804 --> 00:00:44.006
action and plan again.

00:00:45.608 --> 00:00:47.272
Learning reuses the same search.

00:00:48.197 --> 00:00:51.718
Plan from replayed states, scoring cautiously with the median model.

00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:54.596
The value function learns the planned returns.

00:00:55.016 --> 00:00:58.307
Noisy gradient steps push the winners uphill, against collapse.

00:00:58.727 --> 00:01:01.544
The diffusion model learns the elites, weighted by score.

00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:04.869
In the limit, each round does one thing.

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:06.434
Take the current prior.

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:10.948
Weight every plan by its exponentiated score.

00:01:10.948 --> 00:01:14.958
Good plans gain mass, and the expected score provably improves.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:19.618
A Gaussian has one mode, so two good routes around an obstacle

00:01:19.618 --> 00:01:21.011
average into a bad one.

00:01:21.431 --> 00:01:23.307
A diffusion prior keeps both routes.

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:31.201
Pushing a block from pixels, the reinforcement learning baselines stay at zero.

00:01:31.201 --> 00:01:33.714
The Gaussian planner reaches thirty-three percent.

00:01:33.714 --> 00:01:34.970
This one, ninety-nine.

00:01:36.175 --> 00:01:39.444
And once trained, one sample from the prior is enough.

00:01:39.444 --> 00:01:43.367
Planning off, pick and place still succeeds ninety-nine percent of the time.

00:01:44.892 --> 00:01:45.975
Search is the teacher.

00:01:45.975 --> 00:01:47.598
Then the prior can act alone.

00:01:52.275 --> 00:01:55.922
The prior proposes, search improves, and the winners train the prior.

00:01:56.875 --> 00:01:58.941
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:58.941 --> 00:01:59.531
I'm Sheave.

00:01:59.531 --> 00:01:59.826
Bye!
